Shinyapps is a very cool tool.  I've deployed an app on the free version, a toy spirograph <https://viztoy.shinyapps.io/Spirograph1/>.  I can only rarely connect to it and usually get this:

please wait
It's waiting for Godot.  In checking the dashboard the app seems to always be running even if the browser session is closed.  The 15 min timeout seems to not apply. I changed the timeout to 5 min with no effect.

Further, I have never been able to connect from my ipad.  In checking the dashboard, an instance does seem to start running but app never loads on the ipad, just "please wait."

Are there some usage concepts in the free version I am missing? I would like to invite others to try the app.

Is there a way to ensure the connection ceases when the browser window is closed?

Thanks.

From uedbcc711cdbb3da8 at groups.google.com  Fri Feb 13 15:24:15 2015
