I am using .indexwday on quantmod data and finding strange inconsistency with shiny

The code below works as expected, since there is no sunday stock data, the days of the week are set correctly.

I use these same commands in my code to create a shiny web site, and when I launch it locally it again works fine.

but when I deploy the same code to shiny.io <http://shiny.io>, the hosting service, it is no longer correct.  The correct code is: levels=1:5 which seems to imply there is sunday data.
There is no difference in the local version and the shiny.io <http://shiny.io> version of the code, yet again in the shiny.io <http://shiny.io> implementation the levels are different.

I can post more code if that would be helpful.

library(shiny)
library(quantmod)
getSymbols("AAPL",src="yahoo", from="2015-02-10")
daily<-factor(.indexwday(AAPL),levels=0:4,labels=c("Mon","Tue","Wed","Thu","Fri"),ordered=T)
daily

